Your task is to review NES Rename suggestions to ensure they are rendered correctly and are easy to understand. Additionally, you should also test different built-in themes. To carry out this task, we created a playground which allows you to specify the NES which are to be shown.

**Setup**
1. Clone and open https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-inline-edits-provider-playground in VS Code Insiders.
2. Have `GitHub Copilot Chat` installed but turn off completions/nes using the status bar check boxes in th bottom right
3. run the command `Configure Runtime Arguments` and add `"enable-proposed-api": ["ms-vscode.sample-inline-edit-provider"]`
4. restart vscode Insiders
5. you might need to build the project with yarn
6. install the Workspace Extension `sample-inline-edit-provider` (you'll find it in the extensions Recommended Extensions view)
7. Open or create a typescript scenario file `examples/scenarios/...`, move your cursor to line 14 and run the command `Trigger Next Edit Suggestion`. If you are able to see a suggestion, you are all setup and ready to test.

**Getting Started**
You'll find some example scenarios covering many different cases in the `examples/scenarios` directory. This is a good place to start. 

A suggestion is specified using the following format:

```typescript
/*
// <$.replace>
<<const alpha = 5;
const beta = 5;
const area = alpha * beta;>>
// <$.with />
const width = 5;
const beta = 5;
const area = alpha * beta;
// </$.replace>
*/

const alpha = 5;
const beta = 5;
const area = alpha * beta;
```

The extension will search in the entire document bellow the comment for a string which matches the code specified between the  `// {replace}` and `// {with}` block. It will ignore the `<<` and `>>` characters. When it find such a block, it will replace everything between `<<` and `>>` with whatever is specified between the `// {with}` and `// {end}`. The correct indentation needs to be used for this to work.

Create suggestions which you would expect to show as a rename suggestion. Ensure the widget is rendered correctly in different scenarios. Make sure accepting without rename (pressing `Tab`) only accepts the textual edit and when accepted using the rename (pressing `shift+tab`), renames all instances of the variable. Make sure you always place your cursor after the comment block. Trigger the suggestion with the command `Trigger Inline Suggestion` (we recommend setting a keybinding for the command like `Shift + Space`).

